  "term": "apprenticeship",
  "definition": "Apprenticeship is the learning of a trade or craft through a contract in which a teacher or master can use the learner’s services for a set, often lengthy, period. Historically, it was shaped by medieval guild and monopoly laws and later lost many of its more restrictive features by the early 19th century.",
